```javascript
function readSize(env) {
  const size = env.SIZE === undefined ? "small" : env.SIZE;
  return size === "small" || size === "large" ? size : null;
}
```

after:
Check allowed values after choosing the missing-value default.
```javascript
function readSize(env) {
  const size = env.SIZE === undefined ? "small" : env.SIZE;
  return size === "small" || size === "large" ? size : null;
}

console.log(readSize({}));
console.log(readSize({SIZE: "large"}));
console.log(readSize({SIZE: ""}));
```
The outputs are small, large, and null. The argument env is the settings object. An absent SIZE selects small; an allowed SIZE is returned unchanged; the present empty string reaches the invalid-value branch. readSize reads the object without changing it.
